{"type": "message", "id": "fd5da31e", "parentId": "c6096072", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T05:19:28.786Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_a5535476ec8a4c70be1c93ad", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 8th grade math scores all states Kentucky Arizona Kansas South Carolina table comparison points\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 974,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5954864a295f578\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5954864a295f578\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca37fa14d24258e9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... <strong>In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca37fa14d24258e9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce3003ff23963040\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ce3003ff23963040\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f255e2813e28bf4c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults are also available for the 50 states, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, and 26 participating districts. Students’ academic achievement during the COVID-19 pandemic is compared to pre-pandemic performance on the 2019 NAEP mathematics assessment as well as to previous mathematics assessments dating back to 1990.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f255e2813e28bf4c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9db78072f303721\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP scores by state - Ballotpedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f9db78072f303721\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ballotpedia.org/NAEP_scores_by_state\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5673f9f061338ce3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below details math and reading scores for students in fourth grade and eighth grade using the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP). All 50 states and Washington, D.C.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5673f9f061338ce3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ballotpedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42c55fab5ad73356\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42c55fab5ad73356\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3716c04e7f4d9755\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3716c04e7f4d9755\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd98370138c5e8fd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cd98370138c5e8fd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16d1a9a3338c348c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16d1a9a3338c348c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 8th grade math scores all states Kentucky Arizona Kansas South Carolina table comparison points", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 974, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5954864a295f578\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5954864a295f578\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca37fa14d24258e9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... <strong>In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca37fa14d24258e9\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ce3003ff23963040\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ce3003ff23963040\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f255e2813e28bf4c\