4b8155e13f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35649b2464956fe9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35649b2464956fe9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26c0679177b7e399\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26c0679177b7e399\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"2022\" \"mathematics\" \"average score\" Arizona 271 Kansas South Carolina Kentucky NAEP eighth grade table", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 915, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ae161eacb2bc9fa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ae161eacb2bc9fa\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8be5561348c6a7d7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... <strong>In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8be5561348c6a7d7\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"ti