ublic), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9120c3c5dc4f4bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee13052d029c9c96\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee13052d029c9c96\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38a8e075c0b5e6f0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38a8e075c0b5e6f0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f52230fa442b4f9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f52230fa442b4f9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac1085fcb6da6bcb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, average mathematics scores for the nation were lower by 5 points at fourth grade and <strong>lower by 8 points</strong> at eighth grade compared to scores in 2019. Average scores at grades 4 and 8 were higher compared to the first assessment in 1990. Download a summary of the 2022 mathematics results.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ac1085fcb6da6bcb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CON